{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>On a cord of tekhelet.</b> And elsewhere it says ״וַיִּתְּנוּ עָלָיו פְּתִיל תְּכֵלֶת״? And furthermore it is written here ״וְהָיָה עַל הַמִּצְנֶפֶת,״ and below it says ״וְהָיָה עַל מֵצַח אַהֲרֹן״? And in the slaughter of consecrated offerings we learned: his hair was visible between the tzitz and the mitznefet, there where he places tefillin? We learn that the mitznefet is above, at the height of the head, and it is not sunk so as to enclose the entire head down to the forehead; and the tzitz is below; and the cords were in holes and suspended on it at two ends and in its middle — six, across those three places: one cord from above on the outside and one on the inside opposite it, and he ties the ends of the cords behind the nape of the neck, all three; and so between the length of the plate and the cords of its ends they encircle the crown of the head; and the middle cord, which is at its top, is tied together with the ends of the two, and runs across the width of the head from above — so it forms something like a hat. And it is concerning the middle cord that it says ״וְהָיָה עַל הַמִּצְנֶפֶת״; and he would place the tzitz on his head like a kind of hat upon the mitznefet, and the middle cord holds it so it does not fall, and the plate hangs opposite his forehead. And all the verses are fulfilled — a cord on the tzitz, and the tzitz on the cord, and a cord on the mitznefet from above."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:26.109347873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}